{
  "name": "Mutation",
  "icon": "hexalia:mutavis",
  "category": "hexalia:core_mechanics",
  "sortnum": 4,
  "pages": [
    {
      "type": "text",
      "title": "Mutation",
      "text": "$(item)Mutandis$() awakens hidden possibilities in certain plants and blocks. Use it on a compatible block and it transforms on the spot - no waiting required!"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "title": "Using Mutandis",
      "anchor": "usage",
      "text": "Mutandis is ground in a $(item)Pestle and Mortar$() from $(thing)Hexerei$() (check JEI for the recipe). Hold it and use it on any block shown in the pages that follow. Each successful mutation uses up one Mutandis.$(br2)Mutandis Extremis works too."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "title": "Area Mutation",
      "anchor": "area",
      "text": "Using Mutandis on a $(l:hexalia:core_mechanics/enchanted_plants#morphora)Morphora$(/l) mutates every compatible block in a 7x7 square around it, on the same level as the flower.$(br2)Only one Mutandis is used, no matter how many blocks change."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "title": "Witchy Saplings",
      "anchor": "enchanted",
      "text": "Some plants follow different rules. $(item)Oak$(), $(item)Birch$() and $(item)Acacia Saplings$() mutate into Rowan, Hawthorn or Alder, but only with the right herbs growing nearby, and the change takes a little while.$(br2)$(thing)The Art of Witchcraft$() has the details."
    },
